WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.767
Collection should create both usable material and a trustworthy record of how it was obtained.

00:00:05.767 --> 00:00:09.923
Maintain search notes that link each activity to an information need.

00:00:09.923 --> 00:00:13.324
Record meaningful queries or concepts, source categories checked, dates,

00:00:13.324 --> 00:00:16.724
and the reason a result was kept or rejected.

00:00:16.724 --> 00:00:20.502
For relevant pages, preserve the URL, title, publisher or account,

00:00:20.502 --> 00:00:23.902
publication date if available, access timestamp, and source context.

00:00:23.902 --> 00:00:26.169
A screenshot may capture visible content,

00:00:26.169 --> 00:00:29.947
but it should not replace the URL and surrounding context.

00:00:29.947 --> 00:00:33.348
Approved archives can help preserve pages that may change.

00:00:33.348 --> 00:00:36.370
Use consistent file names and an evidence register.

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:40.904
A practical name can include date, source, subject, and a unique identifier.

00:00:40.904 --> 00:00:45.438
Keep original downloads or captures separate from working copies when integrity matters.

00:00:45.438 --> 00:00:49.216
Record transformations such as translation, cropping, transcription, or format conversion.

00:00:49.216 --> 00:00:51.861
Preserve enough context to avoid misleading excerpts.

00:00:51.861 --> 00:00:57.150
A quotation, image, or statistic may change meaning when separated from its page, date,

00:00:57.150 --> 00:00:58.284
or prior discussion.

00:00:58.284 --> 00:01:02.439
Note whether the material is a direct observation, a source's assertion,

00:01:02.439 --> 00:01:04.706
or a copy of another claim.

00:01:04.706 --> 00:01:06.973
Follow approved handling and retention rules.

00:01:06.973 --> 00:01:11.885
Restrict sensitive artifacts, protect storage, and document who may access the case material.

00:01:11.885 --> 00:01:16.796
Do not preserve unrelated personal information simply to make the collection appear comprehensive.

00:01:16.796 --> 00:01:20.575
Collection must remain within lawful public access and authorized methods.

00:01:20.575 --> 00:01:25.108
If a login, technical control, private group, or explicit restriction blocks access,

00:01:25.108 --> 00:01:26.620
stop and seek guidance.

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:30.020
OSINT does not provide permission to circumvent the boundary.
